Drop the fflush of the OVERLAY DATA file, keeping the fsync.

This is the exact defect #437 fixed, re-introduced in the one place that matters most, and
it is chosen over the more obvious mutants for a measured reason: it leaves the fsync in
place, so any test that counts fsync calls alone stays GREEN. Only the fflush row goes red.

It is also the smallest edit that a maintainer might make in good faith -- "fsync already
flushes, the fflush is redundant" is exactly the reasoning that produced the original bug,
and the code's own comment at diskimage.c:1207-1211 exists to refute it.

Deliberately NOT the whole-function revert: that would turn several rows red at once and
prove only that deleting a function breaks its tests.
